321
00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.140
Yes.

322
00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:11.400
It's terrifying.

323
00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.480
It was nerve wracking, but it was also really, really exciting.

324
00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.420
I was a big fan of you guys, you know.

325
00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:21.260
I'm not a big TV watcher in general.

326
00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.400
I just don't tend to be.

327
00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.140
I don't know why I didn't pick up that habit.

328
00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:24.960
I just don't have it.

329
00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:28.840
I tend to be more of a comic book reader or, frankly, a podcast listener.

330
00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.980
And, like, you know, I just tend to enjoy a book or something.

331
00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.020
And I was making my living on TV, so I knew the shows.

332
00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:39.600
But I was a fan of, again, that cast of what we call theater actors.

333
00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:41.940
I don't know if y'all knew that that was y'all's reputation, you know.

334
00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.920
But, like, the theater actors.

335
00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.140
And so I was like, great.

336
00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:45.800
This is great.

337
00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:48.960
Like, you know, Allison could not have found a better spot for me.

338
00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.700
Very nervous about it.

339
00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.420
But then Phyllis was so sweet.

340
00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.300
And we had, like, you know, a pretty funny moment.

341
00:14:54.300 --> 00:15:02.320
I think there's, like, a gif or a meme or something running around right now of her, like, saying some super awkward racial stuff to Val.

342
00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.980
And, you know, I was a class clown, so I knew I was new there.

343
00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:06.880
But I was like, I'm sorry.

344
00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:07.800
This is hilarious.

345
00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:09.420
So we just cracked up.

346
00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:16.840
And that broke the ice for me, made me feel comfortable, and helped me to be what I needed to be, which was funny for the show.

347
00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.780
And so, yeah, it was an auspicious day for me.

348
00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:24.740
Yeah, I don't remember which episode it was, but we were all sitting in a room one time.

349
00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:32.040
And I was like, first of all, A, all of these actors are extras on their own show, which I thought was awesome.

350
00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.680
We talk about it all the time.

351
00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:37.160
Like, one of the gifs, I think, of being on this show was humility.

352
00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:37.940
Yeah.

353
00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:43.440
That here, Jenna and I would have a scene, and Steve Carell would be in the background while we're trying to get our scene done.

354
00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:45.540
And we were all each other's background.

355
00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:47.100
It was really a team effort.

356
00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.620
I loved that aspect of the show.

357
00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:51.760
I just thought, I was like, oh, I see what they're doing in here.

358
00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:53.200
And it was really cool.

359
00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:59.960
Like, that, to me, was one of the coolest parts of it, was that, like, literally stars were extras for other stars, which was great.

360
00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:05.320
But we were sitting in this room all together, and John was like, Amina, so you're a choreographer?

361
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.920
And I guess we had a mutual friend or something like that.

362
00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:14.840
And he just kind of reached across the water and, you know, threw me a life raft and was like, come into this conversation.

363
00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.080
And I was like, that's super dope.

364
00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.500
I am with the theater people.

365
00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.220
And he just gave me an in into the conversation.

366
00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.360
And I was like, all right, this could be pretty cool.

367
00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:25.160
Like, everyone here is vibey and everyone's being chill.

368
00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:27.040
And, you know, let's go.

369
00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:27.540
Let's do it.

370
00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:28.380
Let's have some fun.

371
00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:29.220
So it was good.

372
00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:30.780
It was a good first couple of episodes.

373
00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.860
I found a picture of us.

374
00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:36.660
We were in one of those vans that was moving us to location.

375
00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.260
I'm not sure which episode it was.

376
00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.480
But it's me and you and John.

377
00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.780
I think I tried to do a selfie before.

378
00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.780
Like, I don't know what I used, if I used a digital camera or what, you know.

379
00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:47.060
Yeah.

380
00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.900
But I sort of took a picture of us.

381
00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.480
And we're just all smiling and beaming, just happy to be at work.

382
00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.940
And I just love that picture.

383
00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:54.940
I'm going to send it to you.

384
00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:56.540
I would love to have that picture.

385
00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:57.200
That's awesome.

386
00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:01.560
Because I was so in my head, you know, like I was in film school at the time, like I said,

387
00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.860
and I was doing a lot of my classes remotely.

388
00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:09.220
And so I would be, that van would drop me off and I would go right to my trailer and like

389
00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:11.100
work on something, like whatever it was.

390
00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:14.280
So I was like learning something or another or whatever it was.

391
00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:19.580
And so it was a very sort of surreal time for me because I knew where I was headed.

392
00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:22.260
And this awesome thing with the show was happening.

393
00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.020
And I was like, thanks, universe.

394
00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.760
Like, I've been in this town for 10 years.

395
00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:26.880
What's going on right now?

396
00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.960
You know, so it was totally surreal.

397
00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:32.140
So I would love to have that picture to add it to my memory bank.

398
00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:32.600
Yeah, yeah.

399
00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.960
Well, let me ask you this question.

400
00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:37.680
In Christmas Wishes, you wear a gorgeous gown.

401
00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:38.740
We spoke about it.

402
00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:39.660
How was that?

403
00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:41.420
Because it was?

404
00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.560
So I'm a tomboy.

405
00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:48.300
Like, you know, like I absolutely have always just been like a jeans and t-shirt kind of

406
00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:48.580
girl.

407
00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:51.140
But I love the feminine side as well.

408
00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:52.620
Like I love to dress up.

409
00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.740
I just don't always like to dress myself up.

410
00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:59.140
But so if someone is going to do that, I'm game.

411
00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.700
Like you can doll me up.

412
00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:01.780
You can girly me up.

413
00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:02.700
Like, I love it.

414
00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.520
I just need help with it.

415
00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.820
And so when you're in, you know how they are.

416
00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:10.680
They, the wardrobe people love us and they take care of us.

417
00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:16.540
And like, it is a full blown self-esteem confidence booster when you are hanging out with those

418
00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:20.800
departments because they are taking care of our emotions, you know, and they, they want

419
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:21.460
us to look good.

420
00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:26.420
It's like your hairstylist or whatever, that person that gets into your insecurities and

421
00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.860
goes, I got you and I'm going to make you look good.

422
00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.960
I got, I got you, you know, and that's what they did.

423
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:38.280
They literally gave me the confidence to go onto this massive TV show with all of you amazing

424
00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:43.180
actors and, you know, who had totally done this remarkable thing in your careers.

425
00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:47.480
And here comes this new girl and she's going to play a love interest to a super popular

426
00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.040
character on the show.

427
00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:53.380
And those wardrobe people were like, I got you, I got you.

428
00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:58.820
And they found a great color and a great fitting dress, you know, it hid my pooch.

429
00:18:59.080 --> 00:18:59.800
Oh, stop.

430
00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:01.620
You look phenomenal.

431
00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:02.380
You look phenomenal.

432
00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.660
I appreciate it.

433
00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:09.260
I loved the scene though, where Val and Daryl are sort of having this sidebar and Val goes,

434
00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.420
you said dress up.

435
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.180
And he goes, yeah, I was thinking like a sweater.

436
00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.120
And Val goes, a sweater?

437
00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:15.380
What am I, your grandson?

438
00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:21.220
She was like, she was so pissed, but you did such a great job portraying like so many,

439
00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.980
there's so many layers of emotion happening right there.

440
00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.220
And I thought it was a great scene.

441
00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:27.400
Yeah, me too.

442
00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:28.480
I remember that one.

443
00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:28.700
Yeah.

444
00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:33.960
And it just, what a cute and clever little storyline too, because Val, you know, she really is

445
00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:39.820
that every woman, you know, she's like working in the warehouse and, but I love that character

446
00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:47.700
because she was smart and she maybe didn't have opportunities like whatever, like she didn't

447
00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:51.880
graduate from Harvard or Yale or something like this, but that didn't mean she wasn't

448
00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:56.900
smart because she had risen to the top of her profession and she came in and she was

449
00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:57.540
very serious.

450
00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.660
And I love that juxtaposition.

451
00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:03.000
I loved playing the straight man to all of the silliness that was in there.

452
00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:05.900
Frankly, I could not have competed with the silliness that was in there.

453
00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:10.920
Those guys are all, oh my goodness, like those guys were just, they're funny guys,

454
00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:11.720
you know, they're all.

455
00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:16.840
And so if I tried to dip into that arena, I was like, yeah, no, I think I'm going to go

456
00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:18.100
this way, you know?

457
00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:22.680
And it just seemed like the best thing to do is to keep her as the straight man and as

458
00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.800
sort of like, she's a every woman.

459
00:20:24.980 --> 00:20:26.300
And I really enjoyed that.

460
00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:28.340
My mentor, one of them is Charlene Woodard.

461
00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.920
She's on Pose and everything else, original Broadway cast of Ain't Misbehaving.

462
00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:32.720
Like she's ridiculous.

463
00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:38.980
And she goes, Mina, we play regular people.

464
00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:44.340
And she said that to me one day and I went, okay, okay.

465
00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:46.400
I totally get that.

466
00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:47.660
And I'm here for that.

467
00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.700
We play regular people and I'm down for that.

468
00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.580
I'm down to be the every woman for the people.

469
00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:55.440
And that's who I think Val was.

470
00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:59.680
And so I was stoked on that character and stoked that she got to dress up like that.

471
00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:04.700
Because I think that the everybody, the every man can relate to that.

472
00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.960
And I think that's why people like that character.

473
00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:08.720
She endures.

474
00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:09.960
Val is a good character.

475
00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:10.760
Well written.

476
00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:11.540
Yeah.

477
00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:12.600
And performed.

478
00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:13.740
Thank you.

479
00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:14.560
I appreciate that.

480
00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:15.080
Thank you.

481
00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:16.340
Yeah.

482
00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.820
Those writers were killers, weren't they?

483
00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:22.140
So, I mean, I know you talked a little bit about this earlier, but was there a moment

484
00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.160
where you broke?

485
00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:25.600
Because we would all crack up in scenes.

486
00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:29.360
And I don't know if there's, if you have a strong memory of like a scene where you broke.

487
00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:30.140
Yeah.

488
00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:33.500
That was the moment I was saying where Phyllis and I were talking and she was saying some

489
00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:36.720
really silly racial shit to me, which is not her at all.

490
00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:38.820
And she could barely get those lines out.

