00:45:07.530 --> 00:45:08.270
It's okay.

988
00:45:08.350 --> 00:45:09.470
You can stop now.

989
00:45:09.810 --> 00:45:11.530
That was a great bit that Amina added to that.

990
00:45:11.610 --> 00:45:12.670
Yeah, it was a great button.

991
00:45:13.090 --> 00:45:15.490
We also got a fan question from Neil S.

992
00:45:15.630 --> 00:45:17.050
in London, UK, who said,

993
00:45:17.050 --> 00:45:21.390
This scene opens with Daryl teaching Val how to use the baler,

994
00:45:21.530 --> 00:45:26.850
and the training seems to consist of telling her that it's capable of taking her arm or head off,

995
00:45:26.990 --> 00:45:28.150
so exercise caution.

996
00:45:28.510 --> 00:45:32.490
My question is, was this all the training that is required?

997
00:45:32.690 --> 00:45:37.470
This is the training that Michael didn't have in order to operate the dangerous machinery?

998
00:45:38.170 --> 00:45:39.650
Neil, I think yes.

999
00:45:39.650 --> 00:45:45.810
I think that Daryl really didn't want Michael to use the baler,

1000
00:45:45.930 --> 00:45:51.090
and so he invented this idea that there was some elaborate training to use the baler,

1001
00:45:51.190 --> 00:45:53.830
but really, it was just these couple of sentences.

1002
00:45:54.050 --> 00:45:55.150
That's what I want to believe.

1003
00:45:57.070 --> 00:46:02.910
This Dwight and Jim runner is about to kick off because Dwight really sets up his whole desk area

1004
00:46:02.910 --> 00:46:04.570
in hopes that Jim will prank him.

1005
00:46:04.570 --> 00:46:10.790
He has an open email, he has his car keys out, so many things to entice Jim,

1006
00:46:10.950 --> 00:46:12.770
and Jim realizes really quickly,

1007
00:46:12.970 --> 00:46:17.110
Wow, Dwight really wants my bonus, and he's trying to entrap me.

1008
00:46:17.230 --> 00:46:21.030
That means he can't drink at this party now, because when he drinks, he gets real pranky.

1009
00:46:23.200 --> 00:46:24.860
I thought that was a really funny line.

1010
00:46:24.980 --> 00:46:27.080
I know, I thought John as Jim was so cute saying it.

1011
00:46:27.580 --> 00:46:30.160
Andy calling out their pranking only escalated it,

1012
00:46:30.220 --> 00:46:33.300
because now they're going to try to prank each other to get the other's bonus.

1013
00:46:33.960 --> 00:46:34.740
It's true.

1014
00:46:34.960 --> 00:46:36.260
He's kind of made it worse.

1015
00:46:36.660 --> 00:46:38.160
Well, you know who is drinking?

1016
00:46:38.660 --> 00:46:39.440
It's Erin.

1017
00:46:40.080 --> 00:46:40.460
Yes.

1018
00:46:40.680 --> 00:46:42.960
She's going to go up to Robert California at the bar,

1019
00:46:42.960 --> 00:46:45.780
and first she's going to ask for a cola, Kirkland brand.

1020
00:46:46.000 --> 00:46:47.160
And he says,

1021
00:46:47.420 --> 00:46:50.280
Don't you think maybe you want something stronger?

1022
00:46:50.480 --> 00:46:52.580
You could get that soda from the kitchen.

1023
00:46:52.640 --> 00:46:52.820
Yeah.

1024
00:46:53.380 --> 00:46:56.560
I think you came here because you want a real drink.

1025
00:46:56.560 --> 00:47:00.940
So, he pours a bunch of shots for Phyllis, Ryan, Oscar, and Kevin,

1026
00:47:01.120 --> 00:47:02.780
and he pours one for Erin.

1027
00:47:03.060 --> 00:47:05.860
And oh boy, Jiminy Christmas.

1028
00:47:06.040 --> 00:47:07.240
Jiminy Christmas indeed.

1029
00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:10.620
Back in the Jim and Dwight pranking storyline,

1030
00:47:11.200 --> 00:47:12.480
Jim thinks he's got Dwight.

1031
00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:14.880
He's carefully reading his credit card number.

1032
00:47:15.040 --> 00:47:16.080
Dwight's jotting it down.

1033
00:47:16.240 --> 00:47:17.320
Well, as it turns out,

1034
00:47:17.640 --> 00:47:21.320
Dwight buys Pam a $200 bouquet of flowers.

1035
00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:22.820
Yes.

1036
00:47:23.020 --> 00:47:23.540
$200.

1037
00:47:23.960 --> 00:47:25.440
That's going to be a big-ass bouquet.

1038
00:47:26.460 --> 00:47:27.000
Yeah.

1039
00:47:27.420 --> 00:47:30.040
I think she deserves it because, like I said,

1040
00:47:30.180 --> 00:47:33.140
Jim's going to be doing a lot of out-of-office extracurriculars.

1041
00:47:33.440 --> 00:47:34.380
I thought you would say that.

1042
00:47:35.040 --> 00:47:37.160
Val is now going to arrive to the party.

1043
00:47:37.420 --> 00:47:38.400
She looks stunning.

1044
00:47:38.660 --> 00:47:40.560
She is in a beautiful gown,

1045
00:47:40.740 --> 00:47:44.140
like a floor-length purple off-shoulder gown.

1046
00:47:45.040 --> 00:47:47.520
Yes, we talked with Amina about this.

1047
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:51.480
This is all because Daryl said people dress up for the Christmas party,

1048
00:47:51.480 --> 00:47:53.240
and she took it quite literally.

1049
00:47:53.960 --> 00:47:55.720
I have a catch in this scene,

1050
00:47:55.740 --> 00:47:58.200
and it's about how someone is dressed,

1051
00:47:58.240 --> 00:47:59.260
and it's not Val,

1052
00:47:59.400 --> 00:48:00.520
but it's in this scene.

1053
00:48:00.720 --> 00:48:01.840
Look at what I wrote down.

1054
00:48:02.680 --> 00:48:04.380
What is Kathy's skirt?

1055
00:48:04.820 --> 00:48:05.420
Oh, no.

1056
00:48:05.500 --> 00:48:06.220
What is her skirt?

1057
00:48:06.220 --> 00:48:08.180
It looks like something that, like,

1058
00:48:08.440 --> 00:48:11.760
a kid made in, like, a sewing class.

1059
00:48:11.760 --> 00:48:13.380
Okay, I know what you're talking about.

1060
00:48:13.460 --> 00:48:14.520
For, like, a theater production.

1061
00:48:14.520 --> 00:48:19.220
And it has this giant, crazy, like, elastic band.

1062
00:48:19.820 --> 00:48:22.400
As you said it, I knew exactly what you meant.

1063
00:48:22.720 --> 00:48:26.900
Immediately, it looks like when my sister took a sewing class.

1064
00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:30.000
Yes, it's like the first skirt you learn to make.

1065
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:30.860
You learn to make, yeah.

1066
00:48:31.080 --> 00:48:34.400
There's no zipper on it because zippers are intermediate sewing.

1067
00:48:35.200 --> 00:48:39.140
Yeah, it's a stinker, I'm going to say it.

1068
00:48:39.260 --> 00:48:39.880
I'm sorry.

1069
00:48:40.320 --> 00:48:42.020
Maybe when we get to interview Lindsay,

1070
00:48:42.020 --> 00:48:46.520
we'll ask her about this skirt because, um, wowser.

1071
00:48:46.920 --> 00:48:49.980
In the conference room, Erin is really holding court now.

1072
00:48:50.140 --> 00:48:52.440
She is buzzed and doing impressions.

1073
00:48:53.300 --> 00:48:54.140
Mm-hmm.

1074
00:48:54.180 --> 00:48:58.060
She's doing a pretty darn good impression of Stanley to his delight.

1075
00:48:58.060 --> 00:48:59.800
Yeah, he's very tickled by it.

1076
00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:04.080
But all of this is going to end when Dwight starts screaming.

1077
00:49:04.380 --> 00:49:06.220
He's screaming that he's been attacked.

1078
00:49:06.740 --> 00:49:11.400
And we find a porcupine in his drawer that he says,

1079
00:49:11.660 --> 00:49:13.120
clearly, Jim has put there.

1080
00:49:13.720 --> 00:49:14.200
Yes.

1081
00:49:14.600 --> 00:49:18.160
Dwight is going to claim that his hand is lacerated,

1082
00:49:18.300 --> 00:49:19.280
that he has been quilled,

1083
00:49:19.300 --> 00:49:22.720
and he's going to tell Andy that Jim is to blame for this porcupine.

1084
00:49:22.940 --> 00:49:25.420
But Jim is going to very clearly state,

1085
00:49:25.420 --> 00:49:28.660
um, I'm sorry, but of this whole group of people,

1086
00:49:28.880 --> 00:49:32.720
who do you think would have access to a porcupine?

1087
00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:34.340
It's clearly Dwight.

1088
00:49:35.380 --> 00:49:39.120
Yes, and Dwight ends up revealing that the porcupine's name is Henrietta.

1089
00:49:39.560 --> 00:49:41.700
We got a lot of fan mail about this porcupine.

1090
00:49:41.840 --> 00:49:42.260
Jess C.

1091
00:49:42.360 --> 00:49:43.700
from Sydney, Australia said,

1092
00:49:43.840 --> 00:49:45.780
where did you guys get Henrietta from?

1093
00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:48.500
How much does it cost to rent a porcupine?

1094
00:49:48.600 --> 00:49:52.000
And are there any special considerations or safety meetings

1095
00:49:52.000 --> 00:49:54.020
for working with a porcupine?

1096
00:49:54.580 --> 00:49:57.540
Well, Jess, as with most animals we used on the office,

1097
00:49:57.720 --> 00:50:00.460
our porcupine came through Bob Dunn's Animal Services.

1098
00:50:00.860 --> 00:50:04.820
The porcupine cost $1,500 for one day of work.

1099
00:50:04.820 --> 00:50:08.280
That included the cost of the animal and two trainers

1100
00:50:08.280 --> 00:50:11.920
and the animal's transportation to and from the set.

1101
00:50:12.260 --> 00:50:13.580
And Steve Burgess says,

1102
00:50:13.840 --> 00:50:16.520
we always have safety meetings when we're working with animals.

1103
00:50:16.700 --> 00:50:18.800
It didn't matter what animal, even if it was a dog.

1104
00:50:18.800 --> 00:50:23.260
And the rules to keep animals and crews safe are really strict.

1105
00:50:23.540 --> 00:50:27.420
And Steve Burgess told me that the trainers worked with Rain before the scene

1106
00:50:27.420 --> 00:50:31.380
to instruct him on how exactly to handle the porcupine

1107
00:50:31.380 --> 00:50:33.480
without hurting himself or the animal.

1108
00:50:33.900 --> 00:50:35.560
Now, I was not there,

1109
00:50:35.720 --> 00:50:39.640
but Angela, you emailed me pictures of the porcupine.

1110
00:50:39.740 --> 00:50:40.340
I did.

1111
00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:41.780
Okay, so here's the thing.

1112
00:50:41.780 --> 00:50:44.000
I have such a clear memory of this day.

1113
00:50:44.480 --> 00:50:45.420
Next to Rain,

1114
00:50:45.580 --> 00:50:48.660
I'm the person standing closest to the porcupine.

1115
00:50:48.780 --> 00:50:53.880
So I was very aware that I wanted to keep my movements very minimal.

1116
00:50:53.880 --> 00:50:57.720
And I found in my digital email clutter,

1117
00:50:58.060 --> 00:51:01.320
an email I sent to Ed and Rain.

1118
00:51:01.580 --> 00:51:04.740
I took a picture of Rain holding the porcupine.

1119
00:51:04.900 --> 00:51:07.220
And Ed is standing right behind him.

1120
00:51:07.320 --> 00:51:08.360
It's a great picture.

1121
00:51:08.920 --> 00:51:11.560
And Rain is wearing in the photo,

1122
00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:17.040
these massive, long, thick leather gloves.

1123
00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:19.860
They were specially given to him to hold her.

1124
00:51:20.080 --> 00:51:21.920
And he was shown how to hold her.

1125
00:51:21.920 --> 00:51:23.960
And her name, in my email,

1126
00:51:24.240 --> 00:51:27.480
I say, here's a photo of you guys with Penelope.

1127
00:51:28.380 --> 00:51:30.640
Oh, Henrietta's real name is Penelope.

1128
00:51:30.780 --> 00:51:31.140
Yes.

1129
00:51:31.540 --> 00:51:33.440
These are the cutest names, by the way.

1130
00:51:33.740 --> 00:51:36.820
And also, the other memory I have of her

1131
00:51:36.820 --> 00:51:40.020
is that she loved a snack.

1132
00:51:40.200 --> 00:51:43.140
And they would give her stuff to snack on in that drawer.

1133
00:51:43.280 --> 00:51:44.260
So she had a carrot.

1134
00:51:44.460 --> 00:51:46.520
I think she had a corn on the cob.

1135
00:51:46.700 --> 00:51:48.460
But she loved her snacks.

1136
00:51:48.460 --> 00:51:50.740
And they kept her very calm and happy.

1137
00:51:50.740 --> 00:51:55.440
Well, you know, if you do get stung by a porcupine quill,

1138
00:51:55.580 --> 00:51:58.760
because, you know, people think that they shoot their quills at you,

1139
00:51:58.840 --> 00:51:59.360
but they don't.

1140
00:51:59.440 --> 00:52:00.740
It's more like a bee sting,

1141
00:52:00.900 --> 00:52:03.840
where they'll whip their tail and they'll, like, thwap you.

1142
00:52:03.920 --> 00:52:06.160
Jenna, did you do some Googling, Jenna?

1143
00:52:06.660 --> 00:52:08.700
No, I just know a lot about porcupines.

1144
00:52:08.820 --> 00:52:10.000
You are full of it.

1145
00:52:10.000 --> 00:52:11.580
Of course I did some Googling.

1146
00:52:12.700 --> 00:52:13.420
Of course.

1147
00:52:13.420 --> 00:52:17.700
So what happens if you get whapped with a porcupine tail and you get quilled?

1148
00:52:17.820 --> 00:52:18.360
What do you do?

1149
00:52:18.620 --> 00:52:22.640
A quill becomes more anchored in the skin the longer they're there.

1150
00:52:22.800 --> 00:52:24.640
They have these little barbs.

1151
00:52:24.820 --> 00:52:29.860
Like, it's very common, actually, for dogs to get quilled by a porcupine,

1152
00:52:29.920 --> 00:52:32.700
because they'll kind of stick their nose down and then they'll get quilled.

1153
00:52:32.700 --> 00:52:37.420
The body heat of whoever has been quilled, a human or a dog,

1154
00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:43.500
it causes them to expand and also burrow into your skin.

1155
00:52:43.680 --> 00:52:46.800
And they can even migrate, like, all the way to your organs.

1156
00:52:46.980 --> 00:52:47.360
Stop it.

1157
00:52:47.580 --> 00:52:48.480
And you can die.

1158
00:52:48.480 --> 00:52:49.420
It's very dangerous.

1159
00:52:49.420 --> 00:52:56.040
And so you need to go to a doctor or take your dog to a vet to be de-quilled

1160
00:52:56.040 --> 00:53:00.220
because you don't want to leave any of the barb in there at all.

1161
00:53:00.220 --> 00:53:05.860
Sometimes they even have to do, like, a CT scan to make sure that no quill edges broke off.

1162
00:53:06.020 --> 00:53:07.240
That is fascinating.

1163
00:53:07.860 --> 00:53:08.440
Mm-hmm.

1164
00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:10.060
Yeah, you don't want to get quilled.

1165
00:53:10.140 --> 00:53:12.720
And porcupines have up to 30,000 quills.

1166
00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:13.320
Wow.

1167
00:53:13.560 --> 00:53:14.260
30,000.

1168
00:53:14.660 --> 00:53:15.120
Wow.

1169
00:53:15.560 --> 00:53:19.100
I can tell you Penelope was really chill and she had the sweetest little face

1170
00:53:19.100 --> 00:53:21.920
and she just would hang out and gnaw on her carrot for the most part.

1171
00:53:22.500 --> 00:53:24.060
They're very sweet animals.

1172
00:53:24.480 --> 00:53:28.480
We should also mention the storyline that's happening in the background of this scene

1173
00:53:28.480 --> 00:53:34.300
is that Toby says that a lot of this reminds him of a plot of his latest Chad Flinderman novel,

1174
00:53:34.520 --> 00:53:35.480
A Murder for Framing.

1175
00:53:36.740 --> 00:53:37.560
All of it.

1176
00:53:37.780 --> 00:53:40.760
All of Toby's writing cracks me up.

1177
00:53:40.900 --> 00:53:45.960
I could have seen, like, a whole episode dedicated to his, like, one of his novels.

1178
00:53:46.700 --> 00:53:49.040
Erin has moved from impressions to dancing.

1179
00:53:49.640 --> 00:53:51.120
What is this dancing?

1180
00:53:51.360 --> 00:53:55.180
What is this backward scooch with her elbow going up, up, up, up, up?

1181
00:53:55.180 --> 00:53:57.000
I was like, Ellie, what are you doing?

1182
00:53:57.220 --> 00:53:58.640
I laughed so hard.

1183
00:53:58.640 --> 00:54:00.100
I forgot this dance.

1184
00:54:00.480 --> 00:54:02.480
We got a fan question from Razel L.

1185
00:54:02.660 --> 00:54:05.380
in me and Ellie's hometown of St. Louis, Missouri,

1186
00:54:05.380 --> 00:54:06.460
who said,

1187
00:54:06.780 --> 00:54:09.640
I've always loved Ellie's dance moves in this episode.

1188
00:54:09.840 --> 00:54:14.200
Were there specific descriptions of the dance moves in the script or was this all Ellie?

1189
00:54:14.540 --> 00:54:15.760
This was all Ellie.

1190
00:54:15.980 --> 00:54:19.340
I looked in the script to see the scene description because, you know,

1191
00:54:19.340 --> 00:54:23.060
sometimes they did give us very specific action.

1192
00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:25.360
But this is what it said.

1193
00:54:25.540 --> 00:54:25.860
It said,

1194
00:54:26.080 --> 00:54:29.480
Dwight, Ryan, Kelly, Kathy, and Phyllis are in a dance circle.

1195
00:54:30.120 --> 00:54:31.340
Erin is in the center.

1196
00:54:31.700 --> 00:54:33.260
She is dancing up a storm.

1197
00:54:33.520 --> 00:54:34.540
Her hair is down.

1198
00:54:34.820 --> 00:54:36.200
Face is a little sweaty.

1199
00:54:36.380 --> 00:54:39.460
But the dancing was, guys, that was all Ellie.

1200
00:54:39.640 --> 00:54:42.160
Ellie, you get some applause for those dance moves.

1201
00:54:42.420 --> 00:54:42.580
For sure.

1202
00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:46.020
That backwards elbow thing, I will never forget.

1203
00:54:46.020 --> 00:54:48.180
And I kind of want to recreate it with you.

1204
00:54:48.180 --> 00:54:53.220
I have to say, I really love the detail that Erin's hair starts up kind of looking nice.

1205
00:54:53.400 --> 00:54:58.300
And then throughout the episode, it comes down and it gets frizzier and more frazzled.

1206
00:54:58.660 --> 00:55:01.400
And she gets sweatier as she gets drunker.

1207
00:55:01.940 --> 00:55:04.660
Angela, do you remember our friend that we have in common?

1208
00:55:04.820 --> 00:55:07.040
And I won't say who it is because I won't embarrass her.

1209
00:55:07.260 --> 00:55:09.420
But we were all at a party together.

1210
00:55:09.680 --> 00:55:13.480
And then like throughout the party, she got drunker and her hair kept getting bigger

1211
00:55:13.480 --> 00:55:15.280
and bigger and bigger and bigger.

1212
00:55:15.480 --> 00:55:17.440
And I have pictures from the night.

1213
00:55:17.440 --> 00:55:18.700
Yes, yes, I do.

1214
00:55:19.040 --> 00:55:19.960
And you know what?

1215
00:55:20.020 --> 00:55:22.340
If she's listening, she knows exactly who she is.

1216
00:55:22.360 --> 00:55:23.140
She knows who she is.

1217
00:55:23.260 --> 00:55:23.840
Oh, my gosh.

1218
00:55:23.840 --> 00:55:24.560
I love that.

1219
00:55:26.860 --> 00:55:32.920
Well, I was actually in the scene with Jessica and Andy.

1220
00:55:33.220 --> 00:55:38.160
You know, Angela's standing there with them when Erin does this back scooch dance move

1221
00:55:38.160 --> 00:55:41.560
and then says by the end of the night, she hopes to see them kiss.

1222
00:55:41.720 --> 00:55:44.260
And then she squeezes their heads together.

1223
00:55:44.600 --> 00:55:46.800
I was standing right there.

1224
00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:48.580
It was so awkward.

1225
00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:50.100
Oh, my gosh.

1226
00:55:50.440 --> 00:55:52.800
And it was just as awkward to rewatch it.

1227
00:55:53.060 --> 00:55:56.820
And when she leaves, that's when Jessica goes, that's who you dated?

1228
00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:58.300
That's the girl you dated?

1229
00:55:59.080 --> 00:56:01.920
And Andy's like, yeah, I mean, she's normally not like this.

1230
00:56:01.920 --> 00:56:06.380
But I thought Eleanor delivered so many great moments in this episode.

1231
00:56:06.540 --> 00:56:07.460
And that's one of them.

1232
00:56:08.180 --> 00:56:09.260
Well, why don't we take a break?

1233
00:56:09.260 --> 00:56:12.580
Because next up, Erin is going to tell Andy her Christmas wish.

1234
00:56:12.720 --> 00:56:13.880
And it's a doozy.

1235
