It's so horrible.

1236
00:56:15.320 --> 00:56:16.940
How do you come back from that?

1237
00:56:17.340 --> 00:56:18.360
I don't know.

1238
00:56:28.250 --> 00:56:29.150
We're back.

1239
00:56:29.310 --> 00:56:32.350
And Andy goes in the conference room basically to check on Erin.

1240
00:56:32.610 --> 00:56:34.850
He's like, hey, I think you should eat something.

1241
00:56:35.550 --> 00:56:37.310
And she tells him her holiday wish.

1242
00:56:37.610 --> 00:56:43.190
And it's for Jessica to be dead, like in the ground with worms coming out of her.

1243
00:56:43.390 --> 00:56:47.190
And Andy gets really angry and says, you know what?

1244
00:56:47.350 --> 00:56:47.930
Take it back.

1245
00:56:48.070 --> 00:56:48.850
That's my girlfriend.

1246
00:56:49.210 --> 00:56:49.770
Take it back.

1247
00:56:50.010 --> 00:56:52.230
And Erin's like, no, you promised.

1248
00:56:52.430 --> 00:56:54.870
So what are you, a liar or a murderer?

1249
00:56:55.210 --> 00:56:58.390
And everyone is witness to this moment, to this argument.

1250
00:56:58.590 --> 00:57:04.110
And I'm thinking, if you're Jessica standing right outside the partition there, that glass,

1251
00:57:04.110 --> 00:57:05.130
you're watching this.

1252
00:57:05.290 --> 00:57:06.910
You can probably hear it.

1253
00:57:07.230 --> 00:57:09.190
How are you not like, you know what?

1254
00:57:09.510 --> 00:57:10.230
F*** this.

1255
00:57:10.310 --> 00:57:11.050
I'm out of here.

1256
00:57:11.370 --> 00:57:12.950
Like, she wants me dead.

1257
00:57:13.110 --> 00:57:15.370
I'm not going to stay and hang out at this party.

1258
00:57:16.330 --> 00:57:17.250
I don't know.

1259
00:57:17.410 --> 00:57:24.050
I kind of believe that maybe the music makes it hard to hear around the door and out in

1260
00:57:24.050 --> 00:57:25.990
That's what you have to believe, right?

1261
00:57:26.350 --> 00:57:26.810
Yes.

1262
00:57:27.170 --> 00:57:30.470
But I'm going to tell you what my favorite part of this scene was.

1263
00:57:31.270 --> 00:57:35.010
It's the people dancing in the background.

1264
00:57:37.110 --> 00:57:44.630
Because their dancing starts to kind of slowly disintegrate as the argument escalates.

1265
00:57:45.250 --> 00:57:47.510
It is so fun.

1266
00:57:47.550 --> 00:57:50.370
I watched it both with and without sound.

1267
00:57:50.370 --> 00:57:51.190
I don't know.

1268
00:57:51.350 --> 00:57:52.930
I was so tickled by it.

1269
00:57:53.150 --> 00:57:55.290
Everyone's just like dancing their heart out.

1270
00:57:55.290 --> 00:58:00.110
And then slowly, ever so slowly, by the end, they're just standing there staring.

1271
00:58:00.350 --> 00:58:01.870
And it's chef's kiss.

1272
00:58:02.770 --> 00:58:03.250
Okay.

1273
00:58:03.250 --> 00:58:04.130
I'll look for it.

1274
00:58:04.590 --> 00:58:09.150
Well, now Phyllis is going to tell Val that she thinks she looks like a princess and says,

1275
00:58:09.290 --> 00:58:11.090
don't listen to what everyone else is saying.

1276
00:58:11.270 --> 00:58:13.950
It's one of those backhanded compliments, right?

1277
00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:14.670
Yes.

1278
00:58:14.850 --> 00:58:15.050
Yes.

1279
00:58:15.050 --> 00:58:20.090
And this is the scene Amina was talking about in our interview because they gave Phyllis

1280
00:58:20.090 --> 00:58:22.470
a whole bunch of alts, like in the moment, right?

1281
00:58:22.710 --> 00:58:25.430
These one-liners to go up to Val and say.

1282
00:58:25.830 --> 00:58:28.190
And there are a bunch in the bloopers.

1283
00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:33.670
But what is going to happen is Daryl is going to clock this, right?

1284
00:58:33.990 --> 00:58:34.370
Mm-hmm.

1285
00:58:34.550 --> 00:58:36.790
He's got to step up to the plate here for her.

1286
00:58:37.350 --> 00:58:39.670
And he's going to do the cutest thing, but we'll get to it.

1287
00:58:39.670 --> 00:58:39.870
Yeah.

1288
00:58:40.490 --> 00:58:46.670
Jim is now going to approach Andy and Oscar and Jessica and Phyllis, and he's going to

1289
00:58:46.670 --> 00:58:50.250
show them a vandalized photo of Cece.

1290
00:58:50.490 --> 00:58:52.410
He's trying to set Dwight up.

1291
00:58:52.610 --> 00:58:56.090
I went to the shooting draft because I was curious to see how it was described.

1292
00:58:56.570 --> 00:58:59.450
It says, Jim shows them a photo of Cece.

1293
00:58:59.670 --> 00:59:01.690
It has been defaced with a Sharpie.

1294
00:59:01.890 --> 00:59:05.790
She has a handlebar mustache, a goatee, and devil's horns.

1295
00:59:06.490 --> 00:59:08.470
Oscar is incensed.

1296
00:59:08.470 --> 00:59:15.350
And let me tell you, if you go to the bloopers for this, there is one take where Oscar has

1297
00:59:15.350 --> 00:59:18.250
a reaction that is so hilarious, everyone breaks.

1298
00:59:18.450 --> 00:59:21.210
It reminded me, Jen, of when he did unbelievable.

1299
00:59:22.290 --> 00:59:27.850
But I want to put it in our stories because he does this thing, like it won't play here,

1300
00:59:27.950 --> 00:59:28.990
but he goes like, ugh.

1301
00:59:29.510 --> 00:59:33.730
He has this huge reaction, and everyone's like, what was that?

1302
00:59:34.210 --> 00:59:38.770
Well, Jim is going to do this really weird thing where, you know, Andy says, if Dwight

1303
00:59:38.770 --> 00:59:40.130
did this, I'm going to fire him.

1304
00:59:40.270 --> 00:59:46.230
Like, this is bigger than just Christmas bonuses, to which now Jim has to backpedal and sort of

1305
00:59:46.230 --> 00:59:47.930
maybe say, maybe he did it.

1306
00:59:47.990 --> 00:59:48.610
He can't remember.

1307
00:59:48.730 --> 00:59:49.590
It's coming back to him.

1308
00:59:49.670 --> 00:59:51.010
Maybe he was the one who did it.

1309
00:59:51.150 --> 00:59:52.170
Everyone's so confused.

1310
00:59:52.850 --> 00:59:56.830
Dwight is now going to burst in the conference room in true Dwight fashion.

1311
00:59:56.830 --> 01:00:00.570
He is going to throw someone's iPod into the trash.

1312
01:00:00.630 --> 01:00:02.730
He is done with that Christmas music.

1313
01:00:02.910 --> 01:00:07.950
He's going to put his boombox on the table and knock over all the cups and everything.

1314
01:00:08.190 --> 01:00:09.990
I mean, why couldn't he just place it on the table?

1315
01:00:10.110 --> 01:00:17.190
But no, he makes this big statement and hits play, and I loved this scene.

1316
01:00:17.510 --> 01:00:18.570
This is so great.

1317
01:00:18.690 --> 01:00:23.490
This is going to set off a big montage of gift giving, and there's going to be a lot of rocking

1318
01:00:23.490 --> 01:00:24.730
out in the conference room.

1319
01:00:24.730 --> 01:00:28.190
Yes, a lot of air guitar, very aggressive air guitar.

1320
01:00:28.810 --> 01:00:31.050
We had a fan question for Maddie S.

1321
01:00:31.190 --> 01:00:33.610
in Russellville, Arkansas, who asked,

1322
01:00:33.830 --> 01:00:37.550
how much did it cost to play Trans-Siberian Orchestra for this episode?

1323
01:00:37.550 --> 01:00:44.030
I love TSO and love Dwight jamming out to this song, but the nerdy side of me has to wonder

1324
01:00:44.030 --> 01:00:48.570
how much it costs to use one of their most popular, well-known songs for this episode.

1325
01:00:49.070 --> 01:00:54.670
Well, Maddie, as you know, this song was Carol of the Bells by Trans-Siberian Orchestra,

1326
01:00:54.730 --> 01:00:58.950
and it cost us $40,000 to use this song on the show.

1327
01:00:59.210 --> 01:01:01.970
This song was scripted from the very beginning.

1328
01:01:01.970 --> 01:01:03.730
It was the only song we wanted.

1329
01:01:04.530 --> 01:01:09.450
Steve Burgess shared with me, though, that NBC had a deal with The Office where The Office

1330
01:01:09.450 --> 01:01:12.910
only had to pay 12% of the song.

1331
01:01:12.910 --> 01:01:16.870
So we technically got this for only $4,800.

1332
01:01:17.590 --> 01:01:17.890
Okay.

1333
01:01:18.390 --> 01:01:22.190
But here's a fun fact about TSO, which I thought was kind of cool.

1334
01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:28.290
They were the first major rock band to go straight to performing in theaters and arenas.

1335
01:01:28.450 --> 01:01:30.570
They never played at, like, any clubs.

1336
01:01:30.710 --> 01:01:32.670
They were never anyone's opening act.

1337
01:01:32.830 --> 01:01:36.070
They just were, like, a big deal from the get-go.

1338
01:01:36.330 --> 01:01:38.270
Headliner all the way.

1339
01:01:38.910 --> 01:01:39.350
Mm-hmm.

1340
01:01:39.610 --> 01:01:42.230
Well, now we're going to have a montage of all the gifts.

1341
01:01:42.930 --> 01:01:45.790
Oscar is going to give Kevin a cookie jar.

1342
01:01:45.890 --> 01:01:50.750
It's a woman, dark, cascading hair, a sort of strapless gown.

1343
01:01:51.470 --> 01:01:51.950
Yes.

1344
01:01:51.950 --> 01:01:56.250
We had a fan question from Jessica in Rochester, New York, who says,

1345
01:01:56.410 --> 01:01:58.310
who is that supposed to be?

1346
01:01:58.770 --> 01:02:00.730
Well, I went to the script, Jessica.

1347
01:02:00.730 --> 01:02:03.610
It was scripted as Sofia Vergara.

1348
01:02:03.710 --> 01:02:04.950
Yeah, I saw that, too.

1349
01:02:04.950 --> 01:02:06.430
That is who that is.

1350
01:02:06.990 --> 01:02:09.770
So I don't know if we made that or what.

1351
01:02:09.870 --> 01:02:14.190
I think it kind of looks like I've seen this cookie jar that is Marilyn Monroe.

1352
01:02:15.010 --> 01:02:16.710
That's what it looked like to me, too.

1353
01:02:16.730 --> 01:02:18.110
And maybe they painted the hair.

1354
01:02:18.890 --> 01:02:19.370
Yes.

1355
01:02:19.590 --> 01:02:19.730
Yeah.

1356
01:02:20.630 --> 01:02:23.870
Meredith is going to give Jim a brochure for vasectomies.

1357
01:02:24.630 --> 01:02:25.010
Mm-hmm.

1358
01:02:25.390 --> 01:02:29.590
Ryan and Kelly give Angela a T-shirt that says, ask, then touch.

1359
01:02:29.970 --> 01:02:31.690
She's so delighted by this.

1360
01:02:31.690 --> 01:02:36.010
Meanwhile, the air guitar is getting really heated.

1361
01:02:36.390 --> 01:02:38.470
It is Nate, Dwight, and Creed.

1362
01:02:38.770 --> 01:02:40.070
Then Gabe joins in.

1363
01:02:40.430 --> 01:02:42.830
When Creed joins in, it's so perfect.

1364
01:02:42.830 --> 01:02:43.930
It's my favorite thing.

1365
01:02:44.310 --> 01:02:45.070
So good.

1366
01:02:45.310 --> 01:02:46.410
So much fun.

1367
01:02:46.630 --> 01:02:50.370
I could have watched this montage for a longer period of time, I must say.

1368
01:02:50.850 --> 01:02:54.050
During this montage, there is a fantastic scene.

1369
01:02:54.210 --> 01:02:58.410
It's in the deleted scenes where Meredith makes a play for Robert.

1370
01:02:58.410 --> 01:02:59.650
It's so good.

1371
01:03:00.070 --> 01:03:04.290
He's just kind of gazing at the Christmas tree, lost in thought.

1372
01:03:04.450 --> 01:03:08.710
She saddles up next to him and says, I see you're a little down.

1373
01:03:08.950 --> 01:03:10.650
And he says, I am.

1374
01:03:10.790 --> 01:03:11.430
I'm a mess.

1375
01:03:11.650 --> 01:03:15.870
And Meredith says, how about I fix you some warm milk with some bourbon?

1376
01:03:16.290 --> 01:03:18.810
And Robert says, oh, that sounds nice.

1377
01:03:19.190 --> 01:03:23.090
And then Meredith says, maybe watch a movie under a blanket.

1378
01:03:23.570 --> 01:03:25.490
Robert goes, lovely.

1379
01:03:26.050 --> 01:03:31.630
Then he kind of comes to, and he says, wait, where is this taking place?

1380
01:03:31.850 --> 01:03:34.850
And Meredith says, the Murphy bed in my basement.

1381
01:03:35.050 --> 01:03:37.330
And then Robert is snapped back to reality.

1382
01:03:37.770 --> 01:03:39.770
He's like, what is happening to me?

1383
01:03:40.130 --> 01:03:42.210
He rejects her advances.

1384
01:03:42.210 --> 01:03:46.470
And he says, I sincerely hope you find a sexual partner tonight.

1385
01:03:49.130 --> 01:03:50.210
And you know what?

1386
01:03:50.350 --> 01:03:52.270
Robert California only says what he really means.

1387
01:03:52.270 --> 01:03:55.090
So he really does sincerely hope.

1388
01:03:55.390 --> 01:03:57.690
It's not going to be him, but he wishes her well.

1389
01:03:58.310 --> 01:04:01.210
There's a scene in the annex that is one of my faves.

1390
01:04:01.850 --> 01:04:03.710
Mindy Kaling just crushes it.

1391
01:04:04.090 --> 01:04:06.330
Ryan and Kelly are on Kelly's computer.

1392
01:04:06.470 --> 01:04:07.510
She has a lot of viruses.

1393
01:04:07.830 --> 01:04:09.270
You don't really know what the scene is about.

1394
01:04:09.790 --> 01:04:12.910
Aaron walks in and says, game on.

1395
01:04:13.090 --> 01:04:18.210
And oh my gosh, Mindy's shift as Kelly, where she's just like on it.

1396
01:04:19.070 --> 01:04:22.970
And what that means is that Kelly is going to take down Jessica.

1397
01:04:23.750 --> 01:04:25.870
So we've got Phyllis, Angela, and Oscar.

1398
01:04:26.170 --> 01:04:28.790
She did the thing where you walk up laughing.

1399
01:04:29.290 --> 01:04:30.930
That's what I was going to say.

1400
01:04:31.010 --> 01:04:32.110
And you know what?

1401
01:04:32.110 --> 01:04:33.310
It was scripted.

1402
01:04:33.550 --> 01:04:39.970
It says that Kelly approaches, joins in on the laughter, and then says her line,

1403
01:04:40.110 --> 01:04:41.210
Jessica, did you fart?

1404
01:04:41.530 --> 01:04:43.110
It is like the record scratch.

1405
01:04:43.290 --> 01:04:44.050
Everyone's like, uh.

1406
01:04:45.050 --> 01:04:46.570
Jenna, we could not get through this.

1407
01:04:46.570 --> 01:04:49.190
And I thought there'd be some on the bloopers.

1408
01:04:49.370 --> 01:04:50.530
I know they're out there somewhere.

1409
01:04:51.290 --> 01:04:53.290
We kept getting so tickled.

1410
01:04:53.570 --> 01:04:56.670
But anyway, she's like, Jessica, did you fart?

1411
01:04:56.810 --> 01:04:59.770
And then it cuts immediately to a Kelly talking head.

1412
01:04:59.770 --> 01:05:03.150
And she goes, and that is how it's done.

1413
01:05:03.550 --> 01:05:05.390
And I loved that talking head.

1414
01:05:05.730 --> 01:05:11.250
There was an alt Kelly talking head here where she has a little bit more to say

1415
01:05:11.250 --> 01:05:14.330
about her strategy of taking someone down.

1416
01:05:14.370 --> 01:05:15.910
And it goes like this.

1417
01:05:16.330 --> 01:05:18.430
You don't want to get too clever with a takedown.

1418
01:05:18.610 --> 01:05:21.430
When I was younger, I would overthink a mean comment.

1419
01:05:21.590 --> 01:05:22.770
Get precious with it.

1420
01:05:22.910 --> 01:05:27.570
But over time, I've learned you just want your insult to be simple, direct, relatable,

1421
01:05:27.570 --> 01:05:29.310
and then you want to move on.

1422
01:05:30.450 --> 01:05:31.430
She's not wrong.

1423
01:05:32.230 --> 01:05:33.650
That's her full philosophy.

1424
01:05:34.230 --> 01:05:38.370
Well, you know, there's been a few times you and I have talked about where we're like,

1425
01:05:38.890 --> 01:05:40.570
huh, Jim hasn't brought up Pam.

1426
01:05:40.790 --> 01:05:42.730
We haven't heard anything about Pam and the kids.

1427
01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:44.190
It's where it's Pam and the kids.

1428
01:05:44.970 --> 01:05:46.290
There was a scene.

1429
01:05:46.490 --> 01:05:49.810
It's in deleted scenes where Jim receives a package.

1430
01:05:50.630 --> 01:05:53.950
Aaron very loudly and drunkly says, hey, you got a package.

1431
01:05:54.130 --> 01:05:55.390
Do you want me to put it on your desk?

1432
01:05:55.570 --> 01:05:56.890
And he says, sure.

1433
01:05:57.270 --> 01:06:01.450
Aaron throws it across the room and hits Kathy with it.

1434
01:06:02.410 --> 01:06:06.650
And then it cuts to Jim opening the package and the package is from Pam.

1435
01:06:07.750 --> 01:06:10.590
There's a card that says season greetings on the outside.

1436
01:06:10.830 --> 01:06:16.450
And when you open it on the inside, Pam wrote, Cece heard there was a tree at work.

1437
01:06:16.690 --> 01:06:17.630
Love, Pam.

1438
01:06:17.630 --> 01:06:20.730
And it is a very cute homemade ornament.

1439
01:06:21.110 --> 01:06:22.750
This is how the ornament was described.

1440
01:06:22.990 --> 01:06:25.510
A homemade ornament made out of colored construction paper.

1441
01:06:25.910 --> 01:06:30.470
It's a star with dried macaroni and beans and glitter on it.

1442
01:06:31.070 --> 01:06:33.210
Jim smiles and hangs it on the tree.

1443
01:06:33.750 --> 01:06:40.670
Well, that would have gone to their tradition of exchanging homemade holiday gifts at the

1444
01:06:40.670 --> 01:06:41.730
Dunder Mifflin party.

1445
01:06:41.730 --> 01:06:42.170
I know.

1446
01:06:42.350 --> 01:06:43.130
That's their little tradition.

1447
01:06:43.350 --> 01:06:44.970
I thought I missed the scene.

1448
01:06:44.970 --> 01:06:48.430
And we talk about sometimes in deleted scenes, oh, maybe it should have been in, maybe it

1449
01:06:48.430 --> 01:06:48.730
shouldn't.

1450
01:06:48.830 --> 01:06:49.590
I liked it.

1451
01:06:50.690 --> 01:06:55.030
Aaron approaches the bar for more alcohol, but Robert thinks maybe she needs to take

1452
01:06:55.030 --> 01:06:55.450
a walk.

1453
01:06:55.790 --> 01:07:01.490
He suggests Oscar take over as bartender, but oh my gosh, I mean, he hasn't tended bar

1454
01:07:01.490 --> 01:07:01.830
in a year.

1455
01:07:01.890 --> 01:07:07.370
He's going to need, he needs a mortar and pestle, a muddler, some chocolate shaving, you know.

1456
01:07:07.970 --> 01:07:09.390
He's as a mixologiSt.

1457
01:07:10.070 --> 01:07:11.370
I love this moment.

1458
01:07:11.370 --> 01:07:16.150
I looked in the shooting draft and it said, Oscar looks around excitedly to no one.

1459
01:07:16.610 --> 01:07:21.290
And then he would have had a talking head where he shared that for a little bit of time,

1460
01:07:21.450 --> 01:07:23.750
he bartended in the East Village in 1983.

1461
01:07:24.730 --> 01:07:26.370
Oh my gosh.

1462
01:07:26.530 --> 01:07:28.190
Oh, that's fun backstory.

1463
01:07:29.170 --> 01:07:34.290
Well, Robert and Aaron go outside and they're sort of commiserating over their mutual broken

1464
01:07:34.290 --> 01:07:34.770
hearts.

1465
01:07:34.770 --> 01:07:38.590
And Andy is watching this from the conference room window.

1466
01:07:39.010 --> 01:07:41.190
He's going to start to get a little jealous.

1467
01:07:41.590 --> 01:07:42.010
Yeah.

1468
01:07:42.110 --> 01:07:44.110
A little worried that maybe something's happening.

1469
01:07:44.410 --> 01:07:44.570
Yeah.

1470
01:07:45.010 --> 01:07:52.710
And once again, Mark, who plays Nate, just has the most subtle but awesome comedy bomb that

1471
01:07:52.710 --> 01:07:53.270
he drops.

1472
01:07:53.510 --> 01:07:57.170
He just looks at Jessica and asks her how she does her makeup.

1473
01:07:57.490 --> 01:07:58.650
